ci: make a regression failure name the scenario, from anywhere

CI has been red since M3 and the diagnosis stalled on access, not on the
kernel: the job-log endpoint needs admin rights ("Must have admin rights
to Repository"), so from outside the repository all that is visible is
"make test" failing after twelve minutes.  The step's annotation only
says "Process completed with exit code 2", which is make reporting a
failed recipe - the same thing for any failing scenario.

Annotations, unlike logs, are publicly readable, and a workflow command
prints them.  regress.sh now emits

    ::error title=regression failure::FAIL [name] missing: "needle"

for every assertion that fails, plus one summary error, and writes a line
into GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.  Both are guarded by GITHUB_ACTIONS, so local
runs are unchanged.

This does not fix the failure - it makes the next run explain itself to
anyone with a browser, including me.
